.TH DICEWARE 1 "2026-11-18" "go-diceware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diceware \- generate Diceware passphrases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diceware
[\fB\-w\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-l\fR \fILANG\fR] [\fB\-s\fR \fISEP\fR] [\fB\-r\fR]
.br
.B diceware completion
.IR bash | zsh | fish | powershell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diceware
prints a passphrase made of words chosen with the Diceware method, using
cryptographically secure random numbers (\fBcrypto/rand\fR). Each word is
capitalized and the words are joined without a separator, for example
\fBColtDefaultArousal\fR, unless \fB\-s\fR is given.
.PP
The passphrase is written to standard output. The entropy is written to
standard error, so the output can be captured on its own.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-words " \fIN\fR"
Number of words, 1 to 24. The default is 6.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lang " \fILANG\fR"
Wordlist: \fBen\fR (EFF large wordlist, 7,776 words, the default), \fBro\fR
(Romanian, 7,535 usable words) or \fBmixed\fR (the 15,030 distinct words of
both lists, each equally likely).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-separator " \fISEP\fR"
String put between the words. The default is none.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rolls
Print the dice rolls before the passphrase. In \fBmixed\fR mode each roll is
prefixed with its list, \fBen:\fR or \fBro:\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI completion " SHELL"
Print a completion script for \fBbash\fR, \fBzsh\fR, \fBfish\fR or
\fBpowershell\fR, for example \fBsource <(diceware completion bash)\fR.
.SH ENTROPY
Each word adds log2 of the list size: about 12.9 bits for English, 12.9 for
Romanian and 13.9 for mixed. Six English words give about 77.5 bits.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an invalid option or a failure to read random numbers.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
diceware
diceware \-w 8 \-s "\-"
diceware \-l mixed \-r
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/cleonte/go-diceware
